{"id":4323,"date":"2021-11-22T16:46:50","date_gmt":"2021-11-23T00:46:50","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=4323"},"modified":"2024-08-30T09:53:12","modified_gmt":"2024-08-30T16:53:12","slug":"lesson-2-keyboard-remote","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/lesson-2-keyboard-remote\/","title":{"rendered":"Lesson 2: Keyboard Remote"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221424cc628\" name=\"6a221424cc628\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Remote Control vs Autonomous<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">What does it mean for a robot to be autonomous or remote controlled? An autonomous robot is a robot that can perform an action automatically without being directly controlled by a person. These robots are usually able to use their sensors to gain information and make decisions! A remote controlled robot is a robot that has a person directly controlling what the robot does with a remote controller.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p>Try taking the &#8220;Autonomous or Not?&#8221; quiz below. You will see a a bunch of different robots and answer which you think is an autonomous robot or a remote controlled robot!<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/11\/Copy-of-Autonomous-or-Not_.pdf\" class=\"pdfemb-viewer\" style=\"\" data-width=\"max\" data-height=\"max\" data-mobile-width=\"500\"  data-scrollbar=\"none\" data-download=\"on\" data-tracking=\"on\" data-newwindow=\"on\" data-pagetextbox=\"off\" data-scrolltotop=\"off\" data-startzoom=\"100\" data-startfpzoom=\"100\" data-toolbar=\"bottom\" data-toolbar-fixed=\"off\">Copy-of-Autonomous-or-Not_<br\/><\/a>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221424cc7b0\" name=\"6a221424cc7b0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Pseudocode<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Pseudocode is a helpful way to keep your code organized and it can help with planning big projects like a keyboard remote! Here is an example of how pseudocode might be used.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">if I press \"w\"\r\nthen my drone will fly up towards the ceiling<\/pre>\n<p>Can you think of any other buttons we might need to build a keyboard remote? What flight direction do you think your drone should go for each button?[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221424cc85f\" name=\"6a221424cc85f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build Flight Controller<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Now we will build our keyboard remote![\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">First, you will set up the structure of the program to handle roll, pitch, yaw, and throttle. Since there are positive and negative values for each flight direction, there are 8 total possible commands plus the spacebar for emergency stop.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In this example, the following keyboard commands will be used, but you can change the values to whatever you want.<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><b>W\/S-<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Positive\/Negative throttle<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><b>D\/A-<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Positive\/Negative Yaw<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><b>Up\/Down-<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Positive\/Negative Pitch<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><b>Right\/Left-<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Positive\/Negative<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><b>Space- <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Emergency stop<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;739&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Think about how you should program your if statements. Remember that if and else-if are useful when you only want to execute one of those commands. However, using one if statement and 7 if-else statements means you can only fly in one direction at a time! To be able to fly in more than one direction you need to group your if statements into roll, pitch, yaw, and throttle. For example:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If W is pressed, set throttle to 75<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Else if S is pressed, set throttle to -75<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Else, set throttle to 0.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The else statement is very important. It resets the value of throttle to zero whenever neither key is pressed.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;740&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 4 Remote Control vs Autonomous [vc_column_text]What does it mean for a robot to be autonomous or remote controlled? An autonomous robot is a robot that can perform an&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/lesson-2-keyboard-remote\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4316,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":true,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":407,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1814,1760,1817,1763,1777,1737,1815,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,167,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,2164,2125,2121,2122,2111,2126],"class_list":["post-4323","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-keyboard","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-remote-control","lesson-tag-senior","module-seasonal","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/4323","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":7,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/4323\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12824,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/4323\/revisions\/12824"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/4316"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=4323"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=4323"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=4323"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}